    "description": "Resource Type definition for AWS::DRS::SourceServer. A Source Server is a machine registered with AWS Elastic Disaster Recovery whose disks replicate into a DRS staging area so it can be recovered. Source Servers are registered out-of-band by the AWS Replication Agent (there is no create API), so this is a read-only resource that provides visibility into Source Servers via Cloud Control API.",
